                <section class="content-section" id="introduction">

                    <h2>01. Introduction</h2>

                    <p>
                        Kushagra Innovations ("we", "us", or "our")
                        operates the <strong>SlidePrint</strong> mobile
                        application ("App"). This Privacy Policy explains
                        how SlidePrint handles information when you use
                        our App.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        By using SlidePrint, you agree to the practices
                        described in this Privacy Policy.
                    </p>

                </section>


                <section class="content-section" id="information">

                    <h2>02. Information We Collect</h2>

                    <p>
                        SlidePrint is designed to work primarily with
                        files and information stored on your device.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        We do <strong>not</strong> require you to create
                        an account or provide personal information such as:
                    </p>

                    <ul>
                        <li>Name</li>
                        <li>Email address</li>
                        <li>Phone number</li>
                        <li>Postal address</li>
                        <li>Contacts</li>
                        <li>Precise location</li>
                        <li>Account credentials</li>
                    </ul>

                    <p>
                        SlidePrint does not have a developer-operated
                        server or cloud system for uploading or storing
                        your PDF documents.
                    </p>

                </section>


                <section class="content-section" id="pdf-files">

                    <h2>03. PDF Files and Document Processing</h2>

                    <p>
                        SlidePrint allows you to select PDF files from
                        your device using Android's Storage Access Framework.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        When you select a PDF, the App processes the file
                        locally on your device for features such as
                        viewing, preparing, and printing.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Your PDF files and their contents are
                        <strong>not uploaded to Kushagra Innovations'
                        servers.</strong>
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        SlidePrint does not intentionally transmit your
                        PDF files or their contents to our servers,
                        cloud storage, or the developer.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        The files you select remain under your control
                        on your device and are accessed only when required
                        for the functionality of the App.
                    </p>

                </section>


                <section class="content-section" id="local-storage">

                    <h2>04. Local Data Storage</h2>

                    <p>
                        SlidePrint stores certain information locally
                        on your device to provide and improve the App
                        experience.
                    </p>

                    <h3>Processing History</h3>

                    <p>The App may store:</p>

                    <ul>
                        <li>File path or file reference</li>
                        <li>Processing date</li>
                        <li>Page count</li>
                        <li>Print mode</li>
                        <li>Other information required to display your processing history</li>
                    </ul>

                    <p>
                        This information is stored locally using the
                        App's on-device database.
                    </p>

                    <h3>App Settings</h3>

                    <p>
                        SlidePrint may locally store your preferences,
                        such as:
                    </p>

                    <ul>
                        <li>Paper size</li>
                        <li>Print quality</li>
                        <li>Page orientation</li>
                        <li>Other selected application settings</li>
                    </ul>

                    <p>
                        These settings are stored on your device and
                        are not intentionally transmitted to our servers.
                    </p>

                </section>


                <section class="content-section" id="temporary-files">

                    <h2>05. Temporary Files</h2>

                    <p>
                        During PDF processing, SlidePrint may temporarily
                        create generated PDF files in the application's
                        cache directory.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        These temporary files are used to complete the
                        requested operation and are stored locally on
                        your device.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Temporary files may be removed by the App or the
                        Android operating system when they are no longer
                        required.
                    </p>

                </section>


                <section class="content-section" id="internet">

                    <h2>06. Internet Permission</h2>

                    <p>
                        SlidePrint uses the Android
                        <code>INTERNET</code> permission.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        The primary purpose of internet access is to allow
                        the App to load and display advertisements provided
                        by Google AdMob.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Internet access used for advertising does not mean
                        that SlidePrint uploads your PDF documents to our
                        servers.
                    </p>

                </section>


                <section class="content-section" id="advertising">

                    <h2>07. Advertising and Google AdMob</h2>

                    <p>
                        SlidePrint uses <strong>Google AdMob</strong>
                        to display advertisements.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Google AdMob is a third-party advertising service
                        provided by Google LLC. AdMob may collect and
                        process certain information from your device for
                        purposes such as delivering, measuring, and
                        personalizing advertisements, subject to Google's
                        applicable policies and settings.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Depending on your device, region, advertising
                        settings, and applicable laws, information that
                        may be processed by advertising services can include:
                    </p>

                    <ul>
                        <li>Advertising ID or similar device identifiers</li>
                        <li>Device information</li>
                        <li>IP address</li>
                        <li>Advertising and interaction information</li>
                        <li>Diagnostics and performance-related information</li>
                    </ul>

                    <p>
                        The information collected by Google through its
                        advertising services is governed by Google's own
                        privacy policies and terms.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        For more information about how Google handles data,
                        please review
                        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
                           target="_blank"
                           rel="noopener noreferrer">
                            Google's Privacy Policy
                        </a>.
                    </p>

                </section>


